ens at \u00a31.334m and is fully transferred out, with a forecast closing balance of \u00a30.","category":"reserves","matters":"Complete depletion of a slippage buffer suggests either budgeted spending is materialising or the reserve is no longer expected to be needed, signalling a change in the council's financial planning assumptions","figures":"Opening \u00a31,334,000, transfers out \u00a31,334,000, forecast closing \u00a30","quote":"Revenue slippage 1,334,000 0 (1,334,000) 0 0","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-02","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Reserve balances 2627 Q1","paper_url":"https://wyre.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s33675/33675.pdf","headline":"Investment projects reserve drawn down 94%, forecast to close at \u00a3346k","detail":"Investment projects reserve declines from \u00a36.0m to \u00a3346k through transfers out of \u00a36.8m. This represents near-complete drawdown of capital reserves.","category":"capital","matters":"Heavy capital investment draw-down indicates significant capital schemes are executing; a lender would need to understand whether this improves the asset base or finances an unsustainable spending plan","figures":"Opening \u00a35,962,500, transfers out \u00a36,801,187, forecast closing \u00a3346,313","quote":"Investment projects 5,962,500 0 (6,801,187) 1,185,000 346,313","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-02","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Reserve balances 2627 Q1","paper_url":"https://wyre.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s33675/33675.pdf","headline":"Leisure Management reserve forecast to close at \u00a3254k, nearly depleted by 88%","detail":"Leisure Management reserve opens at \u00a32.2m and is forecast to close at \u00a3254k, with transfers out of \u00a32.1m planned. This service-specific reserve is nearly exhausted.","category":"demand","matters":"Near-complete depletion of a service reserve signals heavy planned spending on leisure and severely limited capacity to absorb further costs in that area","fig